---
title: "Greenhouse Management (Spring)"
code: "HRT-226"
category: "horticulture"
credits: "3"
prerequisites: []
corequisites: []
---

Discusses the theoretical and applied practices of managing a greenhouse facility. Emphasizes greenhouse construction and design, environmental control, energy conservation, and related topics. Lecture 2 hours. Laboratory 2 hours. Total 4 hours per week. Additional course fee applies.
